
  ┌─ Autoflash emulator, for Windows ───────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Windows is the computer on the simulated home Wi-Fi PICSimLabWifi (its  │
  │ "Autoflash emulator" adapter is 192.168.60.10). The device is the       │
  │ emulated stock Sonoff 1.2.0, already paired with your account, at       │
  │ 192.168.60.50.                                                          │
  │                                                                         │
  │ Run the conversion on Windows, exactly as on a real device:             │
  │     python tools\autoflash\cli.py run                                   │
  │                                                                         │
  │ When it asks you to do something to the device, do it here:             │
  │     device restart | device off | device on | device cycle 7    (power) │
  │ If it asks for your home Wi-Fi: PICSimLabWifi, empty password.          │
  │ Joining the device's own Wi-Fi from Windows is not emulated.            │
  │                                                                         │
  │ Serial log: window "device" (Ctrl-b n / Ctrl-b p to switch windows).    │
  │ Device web page: http://192.168.60.50 (or http://localhost:8080)        │
  │ Leave: exit every window, or Ctrl-b d. The device's flash is kept.      │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
